{
  "title": "Momentus Performance k6",
  "description": "In-flight health view of a k6 load run streamed via the agentless OTLP intake, laid out to mirror the NeoLoad run overview: summary blocks for transactions, requests, throughput and VU iterations, then load-generator CPU/RAM, then errors overlaid on user load, then the three NeoLoad 'Values' tables (transactions, requests, errors) as per-row detail.\n\nEvery aggregation below was validated against a run's published k6-metrics.json.gz rather than taken on trust: first build 20260811.3 (838 requests / 969 transactions / 66 iterations), then two dedicated runs that closed out the percentile columns and the error tables. Six rules came out of that and the widgets depend on all of them:\n\n1. Counts and totals pin their bucket with .rollup(sum, 60). Do not switch to .as_rate(), which divides by an inferred interval that moves with the zoom level, and do not drop the rollup from a count, which lets Datadog collapse export points instead of summing their sample counts (838 samples read back as 784).\n\n2. Averages are a sum/count formula, never the avg: prefix. With a scalar aggregator the avg: prefix takes an unweighted mean of per-interval means, so an interval holding one sample counts as much as one holding twenty: it read a true 429.01ms mean request duration as 1139.89ms and a true 355.93ms mean transaction as 397.66ms.\n\n3. Percentiles merge their sketches with an explicit .rollup(900) and reduce with max, so each figure is the worst 15-minute merge window rather than the whole run. Without that rollup the percentile is averaged across 10s export intervals and reads far too low (a true 5372ms p95 on saveeventcopy read as 2436ms). The rollup must not exceed the dashboard window or the widget goes blank: a rollup of 1800 read over a 15-minute view returned nothing at all. The cost of the narrower window is that a run straddling two buckets reads a little low, measured at -21% worst case on the validation run against the -55% to -78% the un-rolled query produced. Widen it to 1800 if this board is only ever read at an hour or more.\n\n4. Metrics are prefixed k6perf., not k6. Datadog's k6 integration owns the k6.http_req_* namespace and stamps its own metadata over those names, under which the histogram's count and max sub-values stop resolving and both reads fall back to the interval sum. Names the integration does not claim (group_duration, iteration_duration, think_time) were always exact. The Min/Max/percentile columns on the requests table are the ones this unblocks, and they are now confirmed: on a dedicated run read back against its own artifact, Min/Max/Avg/Count are exact to 0.00% across all 25 rows of both detail tables.\n\n5. A percentile column is a sketch estimate, not a computed percentile, so judge it by whether each value traces to a real observation. Every one of 81 table cells and 116 timeseries points sat within 0.79% of an actual sample, and each column landed near its nominal rank (p90 at the 88th-94th, p95 at the 92nd-98th, p99 at the 96th-98th percentile of the run). No rank formula reproduces the values, and recomputing them the way k6 does, by interpolating on (n-1), manufactures apparent errors up to 89% that are purely definitional. The real limit is resolution: at 21-31 samples per row per 900s bucket the sketch cannot separate adjacent percentiles, and on 14 of 25 rows two adjacent columns returned an identical value. Read p99 per row as 'somewhere in the tail', not as a figure distinct from p95.\n\n6. default_zero() never appears in a grouped query or a grouped table formula. On a window with no run it manufactures a zero-valued series where none existed, and because that series carries no group tags the table renders a phantom row reading N/A / N/A / N/A with one 0 in it. The plain ratio needs no help: measured on the validation run, failed_count / response_count returns 0 on every row that has data and returns nothing at all on an empty window, which is exactly the wanted behaviour in both cases. The ungrouped count tiles (Failed checks, Failed, Dropped) do keep default_zero, because a single-value tile has no rows to invent and would otherwise read blank on a clean run, leaving 'no failures' and 'query broken' looking identical.\n\nThe k6perf.agent.* series come from the CI resource sampler via metric-forwarder.cjs, not from k6, so they carry no scenario tag and the $scenario variable does not filter them.\n\nThe three '/active min' tiles average the pinned 60s bucket across only the minutes carrying traffic, so under per-iteration pacing they read above the whole-run average: the validation run showed 121 transactions/min against a whole-run 89. The data metrics span one fewer active bucket than the request metrics, so the Throughput tile's divisor is not identical to the Requests tile's.\n\nThis is a sanity check during a run, not the reporting surface: the published k6 artifacts (report.html, group-metrics.csv, k6-metrics.json.gz) remain authoritative. See docs/datadog-live-metrics.md.",
  "layout_type": "ordered",
  "reflow_type": "auto",
  "template_variables": [
    { "name": "service", "prefix": "service", "defaults": ["*"] },
    { "name": "site", "prefix": "site", "defaults": ["*"] },
    { "name": "scenario", "prefix": "scenario", "defaults": ["*"] },
    { "name": "build_number", "prefix": "build_number", "defaults": ["*"] }
  ],
  "widgets": [
    {
      "id": 5014019894902229,
      "definition": {
        "title": "Transactions",
        "type": "group",
        "layout_type": "ordered",
        "widgets": [
          {
            "id": 8054074256633614,
            "definition": {
              "title": "Transactions/active min",
              "title_align": "left",
              "title_size": "16",
              "type": "query_value",
              "autoscale": true,
              "precision": 0,
              "requests": [
                {
                  "aggregator": "avg",
                  "q": "count:k6perf.group_duration{$service,$site,$scenario,$build_number}.rollup(sum, 60)"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "id": 2018461157138075,
            "definition": {
              "title": "Total",
              "title_align": "left",
              "title_size": "16",
              "type": "query_value",
              "autoscale": true,
              "precision": 0,
              "requests": [
                {
                  "aggregator": "sum",
                  "q": "count:k6perf.group_duration{$service,$site,$scenario,$build_number}.rollup(sum, 60)"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "id": 1775661781036123,
            "definition": {
              "title": "Avg. duration",
              "title_align": "left",
              "title_size": "16",
              "type": "query_value",
              "autoscale": true,
              "custom_unit": "ms",
              "precision": 2,
              "requests": [
                {
                  "response_format": "scalar",
                  "queries": [
                    {
                      "name": "total_ms",
                      "data_source": "metrics",
                      "aggregator": "sum",
                      "query": "sum:k6perf.group_duration{$service,$site,$scenario,$build_number}.rollup(sum, 60)"
                    },
                    {
                      "name": "total_count",
                      "data_source": "metrics",
                      "aggregator": "sum",
                      "query": "count:k6perf.group_duration{$service,$site,$scenario,$build_number}.rollup(sum, 60)"
                    }
                  ],
                  "formulas": [{ "formula": "total_ms / total_count" }]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "id": 5959960858920268,
            "definition": {
              "title": "Failed checks",
              "title_align": "left",
              "title_size": "16",
              "type": "query_value",
              "autoscale": true,
              "precision": 0,
              "requests": [
                {
                  "aggregator": "sum",
                  "q": "default_zero(sum:k6perf.checks.total{condition:zero,$service,$site,$scenario,$build_number}.as_count())",
                  "conditional_formats": [
                    { "comparator": "<=", "value": 0, "palette": "white_on_green" },
                    { "comparator": ">", "value": 0, "palette": "white_on_red" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
